  "seoDescription": "Implement the forward pass of a sequence-to-sequence (seq2seq) model using a simple RNN for both the encoder and decoder.",
  "solved": false,
  "isLocked": true,
  "description": "Compress input token representations into an encoder context bottleneck and unroll sequential decoder predictions.\n\nEncoder-decoder models decouple input sequence lengths from output sequence lengths, revolutionizing neural machine translation.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\nh_{\\text{enc}} = \\operatorname{RNN}_{\\text{enc}}(\\mathbf{X}_{1:T}), \\quad \\mathbf{Y}_t = \\operatorname{RNN}_{\\text{dec}}(h_{\\text{enc}}, t)\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Process input token sequence through recurrent encoder to produce final context vector\n2. Initialize decoder state with encoder bottleneck representation\n3. Generate target output token representations sequentially across target length\n\n### Returns\nNested list representing decoded output token sequence.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Sequence-to-Sequence Forward Pass\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nNeural networks achieve their remarkable expressive power by stacking linear layers interspersed with non-linear activation functions and normalization layers. Without non-linear activations, any deep network would collapse into a single shallow linear regression. **Sequence-to-Sequence Forward Pass** ensures signals propagate cleanly through dozens or hundreds of layers without vanishing or exploding.\n\nEncoder-decoder models decouple input sequence lengths from output sequence lengths, revolutionizing neural machine translation. In this problem, the goal is to: compress input token representations into an encoder context bottleneck and unroll sequential decoder predictions.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\nh_{\\text{enc}} = \\operatorname{RNN}_{\\text{enc}}(\\mathbf{X}_{1:T}), \\quad \\mathbf{Y}_t = \\operatorname{RNN}_{\\text{dec}}(h_{\\text{enc}}, t)\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Process input token sequence through recurrent encoder to produce final context vector\n2. **Phase 2**: Initialize decoder state with encoder bottleneck representation\n3. **Phase 3**: Generate target output token representations sequentially across target length\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Gradient Flow**: Carefully designed activation functions (like ReLU, GELU, and Swish) maintain strong gradient signals during backpropagation.\n* **Internal Covariate Shift**: Normalization techniques (like LayerNorm and RMSNorm) standardize hidden states across channels or batch dimensions, allowing models to train stably at higher learning rates.\n* **Hardware Friendly**: Modern deep learning frameworks implement these layers using fused GPU kernels to reduce memory round-trips.",
  "examples": [
    "Input: src_seq = [[0.5, 0.5], [1.0, -0.5]], tgt_len = 2, W_enc = [[0.1, 0.0], [0.0, 0.1]], W_dec = [[0.2, 0.0], [0.0, 0.2]]\n\nOutput: [[0.1548, -0.0848], [0.031, -0.017]]\n\nExplanation: Evaluated dl_sequence_to_sequence under standard test conditions."
