  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef dl_sequence_to_sequence(src_seq: list, tgt_len: int, W_enc: list, W_dec: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Sequence-to-Sequence Forward Pass** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef dl_sequence_to_sequence(src_seq: list, tgt_len: int, W_enc: list, W_dec: list) -> list:\n    src, We, Wd = np.array(src_seq, dtype=np.float64), np.array(W_enc, dtype=np.float64), np.array(W_dec, dtype=np.float64)\n    h = np.zeros(src.shape[1])\n    for x in src: h = np.tanh(np.dot(h, We) + x)\n    out = []\n    for _ in range(int(tgt_len)):\n        h = np.tanh(np.dot(h, Wd)); out.append(np.round(h, 4).tolist())\n    return out\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
